From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:42:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 63/78] wasm32: br_table for case statements and goto state
 machines, inline small copies, direct bf exception flag test

Four independent wasm32 code generation improvements; none of them
changes code for other targets.

1. case -> br_table (nwasmset.pas, aasmcpu.pas, agllvmmc.pas, cpupi.pas).
   twasmcasenode only ever emitted a linear compare chain (the jump table
   code was commented out), so a dense case with N labels costs up to N
   compare+branch pairs. genjumptable now emits one br_table: the
   selector minus the lowest label as an unsigned 32-bit index, one
   target per value (the else label for holes) and the else label as the
   default, so every value outside min..max, including negative ones,
   takes the default. Used at -O1 and above for selectors of up to 32
   bits (wasm32 defines cpu64bitalu, so Int64/QWord selectors reach this
   code too; they keep the compare chain, since a truncated i32 index
   would send e.g. $100000002 to the label 2), at least 4 labels, a
   range of at most 8192 and at most 8x the label coverage, and not in
   procedures with labels (the goto lowering in cpupi
   resolve_labels_complex cannot retarget br_table entries; it raises
   internal error 2026101604 if it ever meets one). New taicpu field
   br_table_targets (one a_br per target, the last one is the default),
   resolved from labels to nesting depths in cpupi pass 2, encoded by the
   internal assembler (0x0E, count, depths) and written by the llvm-mc
   writer as "br_table {d0, d1, ..., default}"; the validator pops the
   i32 index and marks the rest unreachable.

2. goto state machine dispatch (cpupi.pas): one br_table over the block
   numbers instead of a local.get/i32.const/i32.eq/br_if sequence per
   block (the TODO in the code).

3. Small fixed-size copies (hlcgcpu.pas g_concatcopy): copies of 1..64
   bytes that are not 1, 2, 4 or 8 bytes (e.g. a 16-byte record) are
   emitted as inline i64/i32/i16/i8 load/store pairs instead of a call to
   System.Move, which ends in memory.copy, an out-of-line libcall in most
   engines.

4. bf exceptions (hlcgcpu.pas g_maybe_checkforexceptions,
   rtl/wasm32/except_branchful.inc): after every call the compiler called
   fpc_raised_exception_flag, a function with its own shadow-stack frame.
   Without wasm threads the flag is a plain global, so the RTL now exports
   it with public name 'FPC_RAISEDEXCEPTION' and the compiler loads it
   directly (u8 load). With threads (threadvar) the call is kept. Compiler
   and RTL must be rebuilt together: a compiler with this change needs an
   RTL that exports FPC_RAISEDEXCEPTION.

Also a diagnostic in the wasm32 register allocator (rgcpu.pas
do_spill_replace_all): an operand with an unallocated register
(R_INVALIDREGISTER) now stops compilation with "DIAG unallocated
register in <procedure>" instead of crashing the compiler.

Effect on the GocciaScript VM under wasmtime 49 (callgrind instruction
counts, AWFY geomean relative to native x86_64 trunk -O4): 4.04x ->
2.13x.
